WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.960
If you've seen Thor: Ragnarok, you may think
that the movie left Goddess of Death Hela's

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.689
situation pretty clear cut.

00:00:06.689 --> 00:00:10.960
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and before I go any further, here's your spoiler

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.920
warning if you still haven't seen Ragnarok
yet, because today I want to look at some

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:19.810
of the clues in the film together with Marvel's
plans for Thanos, plus Hela's comic book history

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.880
to theorise why there's a good chance we'll
see Hela back in Avengers: Infinity War or

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.380
Avengers 4.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.760
And just to let you know, I've got a couple
of Marvel giveaways running at the moment,

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.990
so keep watching this video for more details
of how to win.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:36.710
Let's start with the first clue that Hela
could have survived that giant sword strike

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:37.710
from Surtur.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:42.370
There's an especially relevant moment earlier
in Thor: Ragnarok that hints at Hela's incredible

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:43.379
power and near-invincibility.

00:00:43.379 --> 00:00:49.149
After she arrives on Asgard, she takes out
the Warriors Three, as well as a slew of elite

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:52.190
Asgardian fighters in an incredible display
of her skills.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:56.160
At one point, though, she gets stabbed in
her back all the way through to her front

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.160
with a sword.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.709
This kind of stabbing would be enough to kill
or at least severely wound any less powerful

00:01:01.709 --> 00:01:06.170
character, but Hela just carries on fighting,
taking out all the remaining soldiers.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:10.280
It's a detail that happens very quickly so
you might not have taken it in fully the first

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.771
time round, but it demonstrates that what
would be deadly to many barely seems to leave

00:01:14.771 --> 00:01:20.490
a scratch on Hela, indicating she has superhuman
durability in the MCU as she does in the comics,

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:23.080
and possibly also regenerative powers.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:27.869
Interestingly, VFX supervisor Jake Morrison
said that when they designed Hela's costume,

00:01:27.869 --> 00:01:31.899
the script detailed that she had to get stabbed
in the suit and then the suit had to heal

00:01:31.899 --> 00:01:35.500
around it and also her cape had to absorb
bullets.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:39.530
On that last point, it's worth noting that
Hela is wearing her cloak in this scene with

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:44.119
Surtur, which we also know from the comics
has an important effect on her powers.

00:01:44.119 --> 00:01:48.039
Speaking of Hela's powers, when she revealed
the true history of Asgard beneath Odin's

00:01:48.039 --> 00:01:52.310
mural, you could see a painting that showed
she originally wielded Mjolnir and, before

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:56.610
that, we also saw her shatter Thor's mighty
hammer, which as Odin once said was "forged

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:58.390
in the heart of a dying star".

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:02.789
In other words, Hela's power is incredible
in Thor: Ragnarok and Thor realised that even

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.340
he plus the other Revengers could not defeat
her.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:10.490
OK, you say, but a stab from an Asgardian
sword isn't the same as the absolutely enormous

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:12.590
sword that Surtur brought down on Hela.

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:16.370
And no, it isn't, but intriguingly at the
moment that Surtur brought his sword down

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:21.420
on Hela, a bright oval-shaped light surrounded
her, which seems a little curious.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:26.940
Hela, like Doctor Strange, has the power of
teleportation and can open portals to instantaneously

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.200
move to another part of the universe.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.990
She arrived in Norway in that manner and,
if she was fast enough, she may have escaped

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:34.660
Surtur this way too.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:39.690
And, again, Hela is still wearing her cloak
when she's struck by Surtur, and if you look

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:44.260
really carefully, it seems like she could
have been using her cloak to shield herself

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.840
against his attack.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:51.160
On top of that, we never actually see a real
close-up of Hela's apparent demise, likely

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:55.010
because Marvel realise they have a good villain
here and therefore they don't won't to lose

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:58.730
her for good or they have other plans for
her already.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:03.430
Now, I kinda like the idea that Hela either
escaped or that her powers are such that she

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:07.660
could have survived that takedown by Surtur,
meaning that she's floating around in space

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:08.660
somewhere.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:12.510
But let's just assume for a moment that, despite
all those powers, the combination of Surtur's

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:16.570
sword and then Asgard exploding was too much,
and that Hela did die.

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:21.010
Well, the thing is, of course, these are comic
book movies, so if the creators want to, Hela

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:24.730
can be brought back, as has happened before
in the comics.

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:28.640
Something else to consider is the Eternal
Flame, which could be useful in resurrecting

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.780
Hela if she is dead.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:35.190
When Hela entered Odin's treasure vault, she
referred to the Eternal Flame as "true power"

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:39.880
and she used it to resurrect Fenris Wolf and
her undead army, plus Surtur was resurrected

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:42.650
via the Eternal Flame in order to bring about
Ragnarok.

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:46.750
In the comics, the Eternal Flame can't be
extinguished, and with Thanos turning up on

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:50.280
his Sanctuary 2 ship in the mid-credits scene,
I wonder whether he could have picked up the

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:53.939
Eternal Flame, assuming it's still burning,
together with Hela's body.

00:03:53.939 --> 00:03:57.799
And putting the two together, we could get
a resurrected version of Hela.

00:03:57.799 --> 00:04:01.360
Or could Thanos use the Soul Stone, which
some fans see as being connected with the

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:04.240
Eternal Flame, to bring Hela back to life?

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:08.730
Next, we need to talk about Thanos and why
he's a big part of the reason Marvel may bring

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:09.730
back Hela.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:12.910
I think we can look at these two characters
as soulmates of sorts.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:16.690
They're both megalomaniacs whose ambition
it is to conquer the universe.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:21.000
Remember that in Thor: Ragnarok, Hela revealed
she was frustrated with Odin when he decided

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:25.180
to rein in Asgard's empire once the two of
them had conquered the Nine Realms.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:29.840
In contrast to her father, Hela wanted to
carry on and conquer the entire cosmos.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:34.010
Bringing Hela and Thanos together would be
a deadly combination as they'd form perhaps

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:36.710
the MCU's most twisted and lethal couple.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:40.690
And it's worth noting that Hela and Thanos
actually got together in Marvel's current

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:42.860
run of The Unworthy Thor comics.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:47.210
Now, I can see that Hela and Thanos share
a twisted view of the universe, but despite

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:51.800
multiple cameo appearances so far, we still
don't know exactly why Thanos is collecting

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:55.820
the Infinity Stones, other than a somewhat
generic thirst for power.

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:59.000
Perhaps that's all it is, but what if he already
has a connection with Hela?

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:03.740
I mean we know Odin kept Hela banished while
he was alive, but we don't know if Thanos

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:08.450
was aware of her ultimate fate and her conquests
alongside her father before that.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:12.610
But if he was, it's not inconceivable that
he might have felt a kinship with her and

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:16.650
would have wanted to gain enough power to
impress her or try to break her out of her

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:17.650
prison.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:21.720
And for the final piece of the puzzle we need
to go back to the original source material.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:26.120
Earlier this year, when Kevin Feige was asked
about Thanos's motivation, he wouldn't commit

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:30.530
to anything too specific, but he did say that
Thanos's motives will be similar to those

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.680
that he has in the Infinity Gauntlet storyline
in the comics.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:38.330
To recap briefly, in the comics, Thanos' desire
to wield the Infinity Gauntlet is tied up

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:41.660
with his desire to impress the character Mistress
Death, who he adores.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:45.860
And he uses the Gauntlet to obliterate half
the population in the universe for her.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:49.660
And, if you think back to the mid-credits
scene in the first Avengers film, it seems

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:53.610
like this has already been hinted at, as at
the end of that movie, Thanos responded with

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:57.460
a smile when he was told that 'to challenge
[humans] would be to court Death'.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:02.940
The Infinity War trailer at D23 and Comic
Con showed Thanos wreaking large-scale destruction

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:06.650
and I wonder if his motivation is because
he's trying to prove himself to the Goddess

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:11.200
of Death, Hela, and to get payback for what
happened to her in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:15.580
I think Hela would be a great substitute in
the MCU for Mistress Death from the comics

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:19.590
as Hela is an interesting character who's
already been established, and that means Marvel

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:23.780
don't have to introduce yet another character
in the third and fourth Avengers movies, which

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:25.960
are already overflowing with characters.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:30.760
Of course, you may still be sceptical about
Hela's return, and it may still be that the

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:35.270
supervillain really is dead and gone for good,
however, when Marvel and Cate Blanchett were

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:39.169
asked about the possibility of Hela returning,
they were pretty coy.

00:06:39.169 --> 00:06:43.120
Marvel Studios producer Brad Winderbaum has
said that Hela is one of the best villains

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:47.080
Marvel has ever had and has confirmed that
she represents all the things that Thanos

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.090
values.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:52.070
And Cate Blanchett herself hasn't ruled out
returning to the MCU as Hela either.

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:56.210
I also wonder whether some scenes with Hela
have already been filmed for either Avengers:

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:58.210
Infinity War or Avengers 4.

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:02.139
After all, reshoots for Thor: Ragnarok took
place in Atlanta which is where filming for

00:07:02.139 --> 00:07:06.520
Avengers: Infinity War and Avengers 4 took
place, so it wouldn't have been too hard to

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:10.990
secretly film some scenes with Cate Blanchett
and Josh Brolin, who plays Thanos, on a set

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:13.240
with a reduced number of crew.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:17.060
Perhaps a post-credits scene for Avengers:
Infinity War revealing that Hela is actually

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.060
still alive?

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:20.230
Now, that would be an end-credits scene to
remember!

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:23.740
So, what do you think about Hela returning
to the MCU?

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:27.680
Would you like her to team up with Thanos
in Infinity War or Avengers 4?

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:31.550
Or do you have any other theories on why Thanos
is trying to collect all the Infinity Stones?

